{title: Oh! Susanna}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - introducing F}
{artist: Stephen Foster}
{composer: Stephen Foster}
{lyricist: Stephen Foster}
{year: 1848}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{tag: beginner, folk, three chords}
# Foster died in 1864. Selected public-domain verses; spelling modernised.
# The original racist verse is omitted. Fresh simplified accompaniment.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Learn the verse with C and G7 first. Add F for the chorus.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [C]come from Alabama with my banjo on my [G7]knee;
I'm [C]going to Louisiana, my [G7]true love for to [C]see.
It [C]rained all night the day I left, the weather it was [G7]dry;
The [C]sun so hot I froze to death; Su[G7]sanna, don't you [C]cry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Oh! Susanna, oh, [C]don't you cry for [G7]me;
For I [C]come from Alabama with my [G7]banjo on my [C]knee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [C]had a dream the other night, when everything was [G7]still;
I [C]thought I saw Susanna a-[G7]coming down the [C]hill.
The [C]buckwheat cake was in her mouth, the tear was in her [G7]eye;
Says [C]I, I'm coming from the South; Su[G7]sanna, don't you [C]cry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Oh! Susanna, oh, [C]don't you cry for [G7]me;
For I [C]come from Alabama with my [G7]banjo on my [C]knee.
{end_of_chorus}
